678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10048,2900,429,400,64,54876,400,65,54876,323,400,66,3,525,1931,5109,1741,429,57960,37018,90,64,15170,65,92,284,1124,37018,35702,26888,90,16,15,3417,35702,26888,90,17,16,3417,3,323,57960,37018,90,65,15170,66,92,284,1124,37018,35702,26888,90,16,18,20,3417,35702,26888,90,23,3417,12947,7379,57960,37018,90,64,15170,66,92,12947,85114,39721,323,24438,551,279,46912,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSuppose that $a$, $b$, and $c$ are real numbers such that $\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{21}}$ and $\\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{\\sqrt{135}}{\\sqrt{8}}$. Find $\\frac{a}{c}$. Completely simplify and rationalize the denominator.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"6fe2123290cbf211f3a8ef9f00889366f1137b7a638b807f6cfb8fa6b81e414f"},"seconds":16.51208519935608,"seed":936202269447213544,"stop":"eos","text":"To find \\(\\frac{a}{c}\\), we start by expressing \\(\\frac{a}{c}\\) in terms of \\(\\frac{a}{b}\\) and \\(\\frac{b}{c}\\). Given that \\(\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{21}}\\) and \\(\\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{\\sqrt{135}}{\\sqrt{8}}\\), we can write:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{a}{b} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{21}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{135}}{\\sqrt{8}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the product of the radicals:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\cdot \\sqrt{135}}{\\sqrt{21} \\cdot \\sqrt{8}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{10 \\cdot 135}}{\\sqrt{21 \\cdot 8}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{1350}}{\\sqrt{168}}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify the expression inside the square roots. First, we factorize the numbers:\n\n\\[\n1350 = 2 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 168 = 2^3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{1350} = \\sqrt{2 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 5^2} = \\sqrt{2 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5^2} = 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\sqrt{2 \\cdot 3} = 15\\sqrt{6}\n\\]\n\nand\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{168} = \\sqrt{2^3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7} = \\sqrt{2^2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 7} = 2\\sqrt{42}\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{1350}}{\\sqrt{168}} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{6}}{2\\sqrt{42}} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{6}}{2\\sqrt{6 \\cdot 7}} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{6}}{2\\sqrt{6} \\cdot \\sqrt{7}} = \\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{7}} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{7}}{2 \\cdot 7} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{7}}{14}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified and rationalized form of \\(\\frac{a}{c}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{15\\sqrt{7}}{14}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{15\\sqrt{7}}{14}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:1137"}
